For the line $bold(u) times bold(r) = bold(u) times bold(a)$ against the plane $bold(n) dot bold(r) = bold(n) dot bold(b)$:

- If $bold(u) dot bold(n) != 0$, the intersection is the single point
$ bold(r) = ((bold(b) dot bold(n)) bold(u) - (bold(a) times bold(u)) times bold(n))/(bold(u) dot bold(n)). $

- If $bold(u) dot bold(n) = 0$, the direction is orthogonal to the normal, so the line either never meets the plane or lies entirely within it.
